@thatguy3000  of course that's a win! I totally get you, prices are shit and stock is even shittier lol, I got the zotac twin edge 3060 ti white edition bcz the whole PC is white and that was kinda the only white gpu version available! Was Hella overpriced as well but was adamant to get it cuz I was specifically aiming to get that gpu.. costed roughly around 625 USD, can overclock it upto 2150 mhz.. and yeh for SSDs the difference is there but very minimal, meaning in real time use if you're not a heavy PC user you won't even notice the difference, Im getting the 3500 mb/s read speed nvme ssd ones cuz the 7000 ones are just ridiculously too much lol no one actually needs that!

3060 ti is a beast even with no OC so dont worry about that, you can check in some subreddits some ppl have it for their 4k monitor and on average does high to ultra settings getting above 60fps, sometimes with dlss quality On sometimes without, but shows how much it can scale, while consuming what only 200watts max, is very very good and efficient! 

And for temperatures you can also always underclock the gpu chip, that always helps but yeah you seem to have great temps anyways so probably wouldn't need it..

@thatguy3000  I'm with you in terms of other models being faulty, i have seen and read many things on such. Mine seems to be the latest edition of twin edge zotac in which is getting very positive reviews everywhere! The 3060 version and the 3070 version of them as well are as great. So what I've observed is that the latest versions of the zotac twin edge rtx 3060, 3060 ti, and 3070 seems to be far from all the issues stated previously! They're probably the best zotac lineup thus far unless they release smth new and better. Though they are excellent already in my opinion!

For starwars, Not At All Trust me, I don't even watch starwars lol not even a fan. Don't worry you can play it right away and understand the jist of it all !!

If you played subnautica before then I'd say leave it, the sequel is barely anything new, just different story and settings. Check out No Man's Sky, you'll thank me later haha! Literally in my opinion the best survival open world game in the market.

